<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dibër</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dibra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dibër is a mountainous region of eastern Albania along the Black <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drin">Drin</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>. Historically it formed a wider district, Dibra, centred on the town of Debar, which now lies in North Macedonia. The Kastrioti family, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>'s ancestors, held villages in the Dibër area in the 14th century. Peshkopi is the main town of the Albanian county today.</p></div>
